From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:30:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 112/145] feat(scripts): route known-red through gc bd and add
 a pytest id rule (gcp-4ngf)

Adapts the vendored matcher so it can ship in the gastown pack and see
this rig's own base reds (gc-cgxps phase 2, first half of gcp-oczc).

a. Every ledger call runs ["gc", "bd", *args] instead of a bare binary,
   so it reads the store gc resolves rather than whatever store the
   caller stands in. The timeout and fail-closed contract are unchanged:
   gc missing or erroring makes every failure NEW and files nothing
   (exit 2). git calls are untouched.
b. Docstring, comment and error-message mentions of ledger verbs now say
   `gc bd ...`, so tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py passes with no
   allowlist entry for the script.
c. A pytest rule in extract_segment. `FAILED <nodeid>` / `ERROR <nodeid>`
   with `::` in the nodeid, optionally followed by ` - <message>`, yields
   pytest:<nodeid> as pytest printed it, one id per line, deduped. Before
   this every pytest red was raw: (always NEW), and extract() kept only
   the segment's first red line, so four FAILED lines became one raw id.
   `ERROR <path>.py - ...` with no `::` (a collection error) stays raw:.
   It is emitted explicitly rather than left to the raw fallback, because
   a pytest id elsewhere in the segment would otherwise suppress that
   fallback and hide it. `^ERROR \S+\.py` also joins INDICATORS, since no
   existing indicator marked a pytest error line red.
d. A header comment records the provenance (dotmill d674c68, sha256
   5567aa79...), the adaptations, and the rule to port id-rule changes
   both ways.

Tests: the 27 mill cases are ported to tests/test_known_red.py, with the
fixtures under tests/fixtures/known_red/ and fake_bd.py reworked into
fake_gc.py. The fake is installed on PATH as `gc`, logs the full argv and
refuses any call whose first argument is not "bd". Five cases are new:
the four-FAILED-line fixture gives exactly four pytest ids; a message
suffix does not change the id; a collection error stays raw/NEW, even
next to a pytest id; a `bd` shim that logs and exits 99 is never invoked
across the module (checked per test and in tearDownClass), and every
fake-gc argv starts with "bd"; and match reports gcp-98gh's pytest id
KNOWN. Subprocess envs drop the GC_*/BEADS_* namespace, per
test_env_hermeticity.

Validation: pytest tests/test_known_red.py passes 32 tests. Pointed at the
provenance commit 37ab7d5e via KNOWN_RED_SCRIPT, the new cases for the
four-line fixture, gc-bd routing and gcp-98gh all FAIL for the right
reasons (one raw id; bare config call; lookup failed).
test_no_bare_bd_commands shows only gcp-98gh's two lines in
docs/design/reaper-budget-starvation.md.

